.Dd October 26, 2026
.Dt GIT-OCTO 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm "git octo"
.Nd manage GitHub pull requests from git commits
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl h
.Nm
.Op Fl hvy
.Cm create
.Op Fl dhl
.Op Fl p Ar parent
.Op Fl r Ar reviewer1 Ns Op Cm \&, Ns Ar reviewer2 ...
.Op Fl s Ar subscriber1 Ns Op Cm \&, Ns Ar subscriber2 ...
.Op Fl t Ar tag1 Ns Op Cm \&, Ns Ar tag2 ...
.Ar commit-ref Op Ar commit-ref ...
.Nm
.Op Fl hvy
.Cm diff Oo Fl h Oc Ar commit-ref Op Ar commit-ref ...
.Nm
.Op Fl hvy
.Cm list Oo Fl h Oc Ar commit-ref Op Ar commit-ref ...
.Nm
.Op Fl hvy
.Cm patch
.Op Fl bcrs
.Ar pull Op Ar pull ...
.Nm
.Op Fl hvy
.Cm stage
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl b Ar branch
.Ar commit-ref Op Ar commit-ref ...
.Nm
.Op Fl hvy
.Cm update
.Op Fl hl
.Op Fl m Ar message
.Ar commit-ref Op Ar commit-ref ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility creates and manages
GitHub pull requests from git commits.
It follows the
.Xr git-arc 1
workflow:
one commit is one review, a commit range is handled oldest first,
and
.Cm stage
lands that series on the local
.Fx
tree.
.Pp
.Nm
talks to the GitHub REST API with
.Xr openssl 1
and downloads raw patches with
.Xr fetch 1 .
It does not require
.Sy arc ,
.Sy jq ,
or the
.Sy gh
client.
.Xr git 1
is required.
.Pp
Pull requests are opened on
.Va octo.fork ,
not on the official GitHub repository.
Each commit is pushed as
.Pa git-octo/ Ns Ar slug ,
derived from the commit subject, and that branch is the pull
request head.
The bottom of a series uses
.Va octo.base
.Pq normally Pa main
on the fork as its base.
A later commit uses the previous commit's branch as its base, so
the pull request shows that commit alone.
.Fl p
sets the base of the first commit to the head branch of an existing
pull request.
GitHub is the review.
Nothing is merged there.
Committers do not have write access to the official GitHub
repository, and
.Cm stage
is what lands the change, on the local tree that pushes with an
SSH key.
.Pp
The pull request title is the commit subject and the body is the
commit message.
The title is the stable link until
.Cm stage
records a
.Dq GitHub PR
trailer, so a subject must stay unchanged for
.Cm update
to find the same pull request, and it must be unique among open
pull requests on the fork.
The landed commit records the review with a trailer, a tab between
the label and the URL:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
GitHub PR:	https://github.com/FrauBSD/freebsd-src/pull/N
.Ed
.Pp
The first parameter must be a verb.
Most verbs accept one or more git commit references: commit hashes,
branch names, commit ranges, and so on.
A branch name refers to the single commit at its tip; use a commit
range to operate on multiple commits.
See
.Xr git-rev-parse 1 .
The available verbs are:
.Bl -tag -width "create"
.It Cm create
Create a pull request for each specified commit.
The commit is pushed to the fork and opened as a pull request
there.
The base is
.Va octo.base ,
or the head branch of
.Fl p ,
or the branch pushed for the previous commit in this invocation.
Accepts options:
.Bl -tag -width "-s subscriber"
.It Fl d
Create the pull request as a draft.
.It Fl h
Print the usage statement and exit.
.It Fl l
List the commits and wait for one confirmation before creating them.
.It Fl p Ar parent
Base the first pull request on the head branch of
.Ar parent .
.Ar parent
is a pull request number, a
.Pa https://github.com/.../pull/N
URL, or a commit that already has a pull request.
Later commits in this invocation are based on the branch just
pushed.
.It Fl r Ar reviewer
GitHub users to request review from, separated by commas.
A leading
.Ql @
is optional.
A name that is the text of an
.Va octo.reviewer.login
entry is sent as that GitHub login.
A name with a slash, or a leading
.Ql # ,
is a team of the fork's owner, when that owner is an organization.
.It Fl s Ar subscriber
GitHub users to mention in a comment on the new pull request,
separated by commas.
A name that is the text of an
.Va octo.reviewer.login
entry is sent as that GitHub login.
.It Fl t Ar tag
Labels to add, separated by commas.
Unknown labels are reported and do not roll back the pull request.
.El
.It Cm diff
Show the difference between each commit and its pull request head,
which is what
.Cm update
would push.
An empty diff means the commit and the pull request are in sync.
.It Cm list
Print the pull request associated with each commit.
.It Cm patch
Apply one or more pull requests to the current checkout.
A pull request may be given as a number, as
.Ql # Ns Ar number ,
or as a GitHub pull request URL.
The following options are accepted:
.Bl -tag -width "-b"
.It Fl b
Check out a new branch before applying.
.It Fl c
Commit each applied pull request.
The author and message come from the pull request head commit.
Approvals are recorded as
.Dq Reviewed by:
lines when they can be determined.
.It Fl r
Download the head commit's raw diff with
.Xr fetch 1
and apply it with
.Xr git-apply 1 .
.It Fl s
Apply the parent first.
The parent is the open pull request whose head is this pull
request's base branch.
Give the top of a stack.
.El
.It Cm stage
Check out
.Va octo.base
on the local tree
.Pq or a new branch named with Fl b ,
cherry-pick the commits onto it, and append a
.Dq GitHub PR
trailer when a pull request is found.
.Dq Reviewed by
is appended only when someone approved.
The pull request is left open.
The message is opened in an editor.
Commits do not need a pull request.
.It Cm update
Push the named commits onto their pull request branches with
.Fl -force-with-lease
and, unless
.Fl m
is empty, add a comment.
With
.Fl m ,
that text is the comment.
Without
.Fl m ,
an editor is opened for each pull request.
.Fl l
confirms the commit list once instead of prompting per commit.
.El
.Pp
Global options precede the verb:
.Bl -tag -width "-y"
.It Fl h
Print the usage statement and exit.
.It Fl v
Print GitHub API requests.
The token is not printed.
.It Fl y
Assume a yes answer to prompts.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
These are manipulated by
.Xr git-config 1 :
.Bl -tag -width "octo.reviewer.login"
.It Va octo.assume-yes
Assume yes to prompts.
Equivalent to
.Fl y .
Defaults to false.
.It Va octo.base
Branch on the fork used as the base of a pull request that has
no parent, and the local branch
.Cm stage
checks out.
Defaults to
.Pa main .
.It Va octo.browse
After
.Cm create ,
run
.Va octo.browser
or
.Ev BROWSER
on the new pull request URL.
The URL is always printed.
Defaults to false.
.It Va octo.browser
Command used when
.Va octo.browse
is true.
.It Va octo.fork
.Pa owner/repo
where review branches and pull requests live.
If unset,
.Nm
uses a
.Pa github.com
remote whose repository name matches
.Va octo.upstream
and whose owner does not.
Example:
.Pa FrauBSD/freebsd-src .
.It Va octo.list
Always use list mode
.Pq Fl l
with
.Cm create
and
.Cm update .
Defaults to false.
.It Va octo.pushurl
Git remote name or URL used to push the fork.
The default is a matching remote, or
.Pa git@github.com:owner/repo.git .
.It Va octo.reviewer.login
Text to write in
.Dq Reviewed by:
for the GitHub login that replaces
.Pa login .
Without a mapping, the login itself is used.
.Fl r
and
.Fl s
accept that text and send
.Pa login
to GitHub.
If more than one login uses the same text, that name is rejected
and the GitHub login must be given.
.It Va octo.token
GitHub token used when the environment does not provide one.
A token in the environment is preferred.
.It Va octo.upstream
.Pa owner/repo
of the official GitHub repository.
Used to tell that remote apart from the fork.
Pull requests are not opened there.
Defaults to
.Pa freebsd/freebsd-src .
.It Va octo.verbose
Equivalent to
.Fl v .
Defaults to false.
.El
.Pp
A token is required for
.Cm create
and
.Cm update .
Read operations use a token when one is set and otherwise use GitHub's
unauthenticated rate limit.
The first of these that is set wins:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
.Ev OCTO_TOKEN
.It
.Ev GH_TOKEN
.It
.Ev GITHUB_TOKEN
.It
.Va octo.token
.It
.Sy gh auth token ,
when
.Sy gh
is installed
.It
the password for
.Pa api.github.com
in
.Pa ~/.netrc
.Pq or Ev NETRC
.El
On a classic personal access token for a public fork, check
.Pa public_repo .
That scope covers opening the pull request, requesting reviewers,
reading reviews, comments, labels, and searching the fork by title.
Leave the parent
.Pa repo
box unchecked.
Check
.Pa repo
only when the fork is private.
That box grants access to private repositories.
Push access to the fork is separate and uses the remote's SSH or HTTPS
credentials.
The token needs no scope for that push.
.Pp
A fine-grained personal access token is limited to the fork.
On that repository, set
.Sy Pull requests
and
.Sy Issues
to read and write, and
.Sy Contents
to read.
.Sy Metadata
read is included with those.
Pull requests covers
.Cm create
and review requests.
Issues covers comments and labels.
Contents covers reading the head commit.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a classic personal access token.
The form is
.Lk https://github.com/settings/tokens/new .
Sign in, name the token, and check
.Pa public_repo .
Check
.Pa repo
instead when the fork is private.
Generate the token.
GitHub shows the value once.
That value is
.Ev TOKEN
below.
Point
.Nm
at a fork, store it, and create a pull request from
.Dv HEAD :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ git remote add github git@github.com:FrauBSD/freebsd-src.git
$ git config --global octo.fork FrauBSD/freebsd-src
$ git config --global octo.token TOKEN
$ git commit -m "kern: Rewrite in Rust"
$ git octo create HEAD
.Ed
.Pp
Amend that commit and update the pull request:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ git commit --amend
$ git octo update HEAD
.Ed
.Pp
Land it on the local tree and push with the SSH remote.
The GitHub pull request stays open as the review:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ git octo stage HEAD
$ git push freebsd HEAD:main
.Ed
.Pp
Request a reviewer while creating:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ git octo create -r markj HEAD
.Ed
.Pp
Create one pull request per commit in a range.
The first commit in the range is excluded, as with
.Xr git-rev-list 1 .
Each later pull request is based on the branch pushed for the
commit before it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ git octo create HEAD~3..HEAD
.Ed
.Pp
Base one commit on an existing pull request:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ git octo create -p 12 HEAD
.Ed
.Pp
Show what an update of
.Dv HEAD
would change:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ git octo diff HEAD
.Ed
.Pp
Apply pull request 12345 and commit it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ git octo patch -c 12345
.Ed
.Pp
List pull requests for a branch:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ git octo list main..feature
.Ed
.Sh LIMITATIONS
.Nm
uses the
.Xr git-arc 1
verbs.
The review workflow differs as follows.
.Bl -tag -width "Reviewers"
.It Reviews
Pull requests are opened on
.Va octo.fork .
They are not Differential Revisions, and they are not opened on
the official GitHub repository.
Phabricator mail rules do not see them.
Someone is told about a review when named with
.Fl r
or
.Fl s ,
or when they already watch the fork.
.Cm stage
prepares the local tree.
The push into
.Fx
is still the SSH remote.
.It Numbers
Phabricator's
.Ql D1234
is one id for the whole project, and
.Xr git-arc 1
accepts that form.
.Nm
does not accept it.
A pull request number belongs to one repository.
In a comment or pull request body on the fork,
.Ql #12
and
.Ql GH-12
link to pull request 12 there.
A review in another repository is written
.Ql owner/repo#12 .
.It Stacks
.Fl p
sets the new pull request's base to the parent review's branch
on the fork.
That branch, and
.Va octo.base ,
must already exist on the fork.
.Cm patch Fl s
follows that base branch.
Each review also keeps a
.Pa git-octo/ Ns Ar slug
branch.
.Cm create
stops if that branch name is already present.
.Cm update
force-pushes it.
Without the branch,
.Cm update
and
.Cm diff
have no head to fetch.
.It Trailers
.Cm stage
writes
.Dq GitHub PR ,
a tab, and the pull request URL.
.Dq Reviewed by
is written only for people who approved.
By default the name is the GitHub login.
.Va octo.reviewer.login
can replace that login with other text.
In the setting below,
.Ql devinteske
is the GitHub handle, and
.Ql dteske
is the FreeBSD handle written into the trailer:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ git config octo.reviewer.devinteske dteske
.Ed
.Pp
An approval by that account is then recorded as
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Reviewed by:	dteske
.Ed
.Pp
Without that setting the same approval is recorded as
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Reviewed by:	devinteske
.Ed
.Pp
If nobody approved, that trailer is omitted.
.It Reviewers
.Fl r
names GitHub users, or teams when the fork owner is an
organization.
.Fl s
posts a comment of the form
.Ql cc @user .
GitHub does not keep a separate subscriber list for that user.
.Fl t
adds labels that already exist on the fork.
.It Update
.Cm update
replaces the branch tip and adds a comment.
It leaves the pull request title and body as they were at
.Cm create .
Until a
.Dq GitHub PR
trailer is present, a commit is found by its subject, so a new
subject is a different review.
.It Diff
.Cm diff
compares the tree of the pull request head with the tree of the
local commit.
.Nm git arc
applies the review's raw diff to the commit's parent and compares
that with the commit, so a rebase can still match.
After a rebase,
.Nm
also shows upstream changes that are not part of the review.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fetch 1 ,
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr git-arc 1 ,
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr build 7 ,
